From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -bank_column_layout, a word's bits
 contiguous
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With banks a row holds -bank_columns words, laid out as the column mux
lays out its words: bit by bit, interleaved. Each word is decoded whole,
so nothing reads the row through a mux, and the interleave only costs:
a word's selects and write enables run the whole row to reach its bits.
-bank_column_layout contiguous puts each word's bits side by side with
its select column after them; the per-bit read trees cross the row
instead. XiangShan's RobEntryFile (352 words of 21 bits, 16 read and 8
write ports, 4 words a row) had rows 278 um wide: dissolved into a
parent, the resizer found 6,483 slew violations on those nets and put
6,043 buffers inside the full array, which detailed placement could not
legalize. Default: interleaved, as before.

Tested: src/ram/test/bank_column_layout_asap7.tcl.

Commit 16 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
